Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:08:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Drop a fragment job's reference on
 its geometry job

Once rendering works on the iPad 5, every fragment job warns at
WARN_ON(job->paired_job) in pvr_job.c, thousands of times a minute.
Geometry jobs are never freed, and clients hang when destroying a
render target: glmark2 and vkcube run until killed.

Apple queues receive jobs linked by pvr_jobs_link_geom_frag(), but their
free path does not drop the fragment job's paired geometry reference.
That reference also keeps the geometry job's HWRT and context alive.

Follow pvr_queue_free_job(): drop the paired geometry reference and
clear paired_job before dropping the scheduler's reference.

Affects the shared Apple queue used by the A9 (S8003) and A10 (T8010).
The A10 has been build-tested only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_queue.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_queue.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_queue.c
index 80bc17b..d176fe6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_queue.c
@@ -89,6 +89,11 @@ static void pvr_apple_free_job(struct drm_sched_job *sched_job)
 	struct pvr_job *job = container_of(sched_job, struct pvr_job, base);
 
 	drm_sched_job_cleanup(sched_job);
+
+	if (job->type == DRM_PVR_JOB_TYPE_FRAGMENT && job->paired_job)
+		pvr_job_put(job->paired_job);
+
+	job->paired_job = NULL;
 	pvr_job_put(job);
 }
 

